pull/102784#pullrequestreview-2619546462","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102784","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102784#pullrequestreview-2619546462"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102784"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-16T06:05:53Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2619949056,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6cKUAA","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"At least I think it is wrong to call a transition for something without a connection with a method called travel.\r\n\r\nI thought about using the term queue too like `teleport(String p_state, bool p_queue)`, but I think there is a concern about teleport between states with paths if you put the travel path and teleport requests in the same queue.\r\n\r\nSo what you are trying to do now is say that both of the following states are handled equally and they cannot use teleport_transition.\r\n\r\n- `queue[A(travel), B(travel), C(travel)]`\r\n- `queue[A(travel), B(teleport), C(teleport)]`\r\n\r\nThis means that teleport_transition is not available between states that are connected, which may be confusing. At least a warning is needed in `teleport()` if they are connected.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, the element travel path queue should have a flag indicating that it is a path by teleport, and `teleport_transition` should take precedence if the path is connected.\r\n\r\nHowever, there is a concern that the above would make teleport only too sophisticated and make `travel()` unnecessary.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nSo, for the sake of generalization, I have come up with the following method. How about it?\r\n\r\n- The transition name is `default_transition`\r\n- Add `queue(String p_state)`\r\n  - Add `p_state` to the `travel_path` array. If there is no connection, `default_transition` is used.\r\n- Add `queue_travel(String p_state)`\r\n  - Concatenates the A* path from the last element of the `travel_path` array to `p_state`. If `travel_path` is empty, it is equivalent to `travel()`.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102784#pullrequestreview-2619949056","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102784","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102784#pullrequestreview-2619949056"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102784"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-17T04:09:00Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2619963377,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6cKXfx","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.c